The sign trichotomy requires 17,140 Work, 52,332 staged bytes and 192 returned bytes for admission, with three exact cells. Reusing that contract with the worked negative box costs 5,388 Work and 47,920 staged bytes. These are the complete admission and reuse lifecycles (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`), (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`), pinned by literal resource tests (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`).

**Example (Phase partition costs)** · `ex:cas:decision-partition-phase-costs`

The seven phase charts require 48,944 Work, 67,112 staged bytes and 256 returned bytes for admission, with nine exact Cartesian cells. Reusing that contract with the upper-left rectangle costs 10,420 Work and 55,248 staged bytes. These are the complete admission and reuse lifecycles (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`), (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`), pinned by literal resource tests (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`).

**Rule (Finite partition resource ownership)** · `rule:cas:decision-partition-resources`

Work and staging cover traversal, total affine reconstruction, exact cuts, cell ownership and retained copies. Returned and caller-retained bytes are the same bound; added graph bytes and reuse output are zero. Reuse staging includes the retained contract plus the full current box-cut scratch (`rule:cas:decision-partition-reuse`). These thresholds are conservative accounted bounds, not allocator measurements. Literal N/N−1 tests pin admission Work, staging, output and Cartesian cells, prior Work and one retained input byte (`test:integration:decision-partition-resource-boundaries`); reuse Work, staging and cumulative exhaustion (`test:integration:decision-partition-reuse-boundaries`); and combined admission/reuse with atomic refusal and a widened box (`test:integration:decision-partition-atomic-lifecycle`). No permanent test searches a byte threshold, and spent Work remains spent on refusal.

**Definition (Closed rational enclosure contract)** · `def:cas:decision-enclosure-contract`

`nrz_cas::decision::RationalEnclosure` names the original `target`, exact `context`, that context's actual `input_family`, rational `lower` and `upper`, and an `EnclosureOrigin`. `ExactRational { expression, value }` proposes an exact rational result; `PiBound { expression, certificate }` supplies the independent constant theorem of (`rule:cas:pi-machin-certificates`). Both require the identical original expression. `Cas::check_rational_enclosure` returns a sealed `CheckedRationalEnclosure` retaining the complete contract, constant theorem dependency and logical ownership bound. Context identity remains part of the contract even though a closed target needs no input assumption (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-qualified-family`).

**Rule (Closed original-expression replay)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-replay`

The checker delegates to `ExactConstant::from_expression`, which inspects every original operand, establishes finite-real divisor domains before normalization and independently checks equality to the normalized result. `ExactRational` requires an exactly rational result equal to its candidate; exact cancellation such as `Pi/Pi` needs no constant bound (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-named-constant-boundary`). `PiBound` independently validates the finite Machin certificate and propagates closed rational intervals through normalized negation, addition, subtraction, multiplication, division and integer powers; every interval divisor must exclude zero (`test:integration:decision-pi-closed-targets`). Both routes check containment in the requested box, with no floating comparisons (`rule:cas:pi-machin-certificates`).

**Rule (Closed replay refusals)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-refusals`

Foreign replay handles, another target and a false rational result refuse (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-original-target`); reversed or excluding boxes refuse (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-false-boxes`); substituting a wider input family refuses (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-qualified-family`). `ScalarKernel`, `MatrixKernel` and `Unverified` origins return `UnsupportedCertificate` (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-unsupported-origins`). A hidden zero divisor remains `RefutedDomain` even under multiplication by zero or quotient cancellation (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-hidden-domain`). Free inputs, including a canceled free input, remain unsupported (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-free-input-boundary`).

**Rule (Closed enclosure authority)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-authority`

The sealed enclosure checks the supported closed target on the exact retained family; it establishes neither family nonemptiness nor context consistency. Alone it creates no witness, local frame, hypothesis or portable proof, and cannot connect a closed target to a separate case coordinate (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-no-membership-authority`). A separate `DecisionIntroduction` requires exact source equalities and a complete partition before introducing certified membership (`def:cas:decision-introduction-contract`). The admitted π remainder theorem is independently checked; free-input interval arguments and scalar or matrix origins remain unsupported (`rule:cas:pi-machin-certificates`), (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-unsupported-origins`).

**Example (Closed rational decision targets)** · `ex:cas:decision-enclosure-examples`

The original driven expression `1000*(1/40)-1/(1000*(1/100000))` normalizes exactly to −75 inside `[−301/4,−299/4]`; the nominal phase components −3/2 and 3/8 pass their boxes (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-closed-examples`). The actual LC target `10/Pi` now replays inside `[203/64,205/64]` through the checked π interval `[640/205,640/203]` (`test:integration:decision-pi-closed-targets`). The complete LC enclosure costs 57,786 Work and returns 1,336 logical bytes, with literal N/N−1 and prior-Work boundaries (`test:integration:decision-pi-costs`), (`test:integration:decision-pi-resources`). Supplying only the rational candidate 51/16 still refuses after 28,201 Work; a missing, inward, nominal-only or too-wide π certificate cannot prove the target box (`test:integration:decision-pi-refusals`).

**Example (Closed sign replay costs)** · `ex:cas:decision-enclosure-sign-costs`

Replaying the original driven rational expression costs 53,628 Work, 29,187 staged bytes, 5,696 temporary private-graph payload bytes and 800 returned/retained bytes. The caller's graph remains unchanged. These are complete original-target replay costs for the sign reference (`ex:cas:decision-enclosure-examples`), pinned at literal N/N−1 boundaries (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-resource-boundaries`).

**Example (Closed phase component replay costs)** · `ex:cas:decision-enclosure-phase-costs`

The nominal real component −3/2 costs 8,785 Work and the nominal imaginary component 3/8 costs 9,361 Work. Each separately requires 22,856 staged bytes, 1,539 temporary private-graph payload bytes and 792 returned/retained bytes. These measurements authenticate the original component targets (`ex:cas:decision-enclosure-examples`); they exclude a Complex projection theorem, joint retained-result storage and chart introduction. Each boundary is pinned independently (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-resource-boundaries`).

**Rule (Closed replay lifecycle accounting)** · `rule:cas:decision-enclosure-resources`

The caller's cumulative ledger pays for retained request ownership, bounded rational scratch, temporary exact-constant graph construction, original-domain checking, normalization equality, endpoint comparisons and copying the returned contract. The returned ownership excludes shared source syntax; temporary private graph payload is distinct from new caller graph bytes, which are zero. No cache is consulted. Work stays spent on refusal and temporary limits are restored; literal tests cover prior Work, one retained input byte, repeated replay and exhausted replay with unchanged graph occupancy (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-resource-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-enclosure-cumulative-ledger`).

**Assumption (Certified region membership)** · `assum:cas:hyp-certified-region-membership`

Formal hypothesis `hyp.certified-region-membership`, version 1. The exact source family belongs to the selected option under a retained checked introduction. Required premises: Exact introducing context and slot, partition, replay, cut and coordinate-to-target equality proofs with their used source hypotheses. Standing: Hypothesis; every undischarged use remains conditional.

**Theorem (Enclosure membership introduction)** · `thm:cas:decision-enclosure-membership`

Formal schema `decision.enclosure-membership`, version 1. Exact target enclosures and box inclusion establish membership in the declared option. Required premises: Complete partition, exact original-target replay, cut and ordered coordinate-to-target equalities on the whole source family, retaining every used hypothesis. Standing: Lemma; instances are CAS-checked.

**Definition (Checked decision introduction contract)** · `def:cas:decision-introduction-contract`

`DecisionIntroduction { partition, cut, enclosures }` is the untrusted payload of `Certificate::Decision`, checked by `Primitive::RegionDecide`. Its expected conclusion is `Statement::Subset` from the exact source family's region to the actual selected association region. Ordered proof premises establish each coordinate equal to its closed target by a `DefinedAndEqual` equality or an exact `Equal` predicate fact on that whole family. The source context, endpoints, ordered axes, case and integer declarations must agree. Every premise is discharged relative to its retained hypotheses; full partition, cut and original-target replay run before proof publication (`thm:cas:decision-enclosure-membership`), (`test:integration:decision-introduction-rejects-incomplete-evidence`).

**Rule (Certified local frame and proof identity)** · `rule:cas:decision-certified-frame`

`ContextDraft::Certified { parent, region, introduction }` accepts only the exact earlier checked decision proof. Its local membership slot zero classifies as `CertifiedRegionMembership`; ordinary `ContextDraft::Local` remains `RegionMembership`. Admission retains the introduction dependency and interns by its full proof identity, including the source proofs. Identical frames reuse their existing record, while different source proof roots remain distinct (`test:integration:decision-certified-proof-identity`). Source assumptions survive membership use, wire replay and `Cas::proof_citations`; `ProofCitation::auxiliary_schema` identifies the retained decision schema (`test:integration:decision-certified-citation-closure`), (`test:integration:decision-introduction-register`).

**Rule (Certified introduction refusals and supported family)** · `rule:cas:decision-introduction-refusals`

This introduction subset requires the source family's exact region to equal the admitted case domain, whose nonemptiness follows from partition checking (`rule:cas:decision-partition-admission`). Missing source equalities, unrelated replay targets, unsupported origins and mismatched coordinate boxes refuse (`test:integration:decision-introduction-rejects-incomplete-evidence`). Widened families or option conclusions refuse (`test:integration:decision-introduction-rejects-widening`); escaped slots, sibling frames and ordinary proofs cannot impersonate a certified frame (`test:integration:decision-certified-frame-refusals`). Changing the parent or selected option of a valid introduction refuses (`test:integration:decision-certified-frame-contract`). Membership cannot be recast as an elimination cover (`test:integration:decision-introduction-is-not-a-cover`).

**Rule (Portable certified frame schema)** · `rule:cas:decision-introduction-wire`

The current witness format carries certified contexts in record tag 37 and the closed decision certificate in certificate tag 14 with semantic version 1. The context references an earlier application record; import independently reconstructs that introduction before admitting the frame, then verifies the exact header and meet region. The certificate retains the whole partition contract, cut and original enclosure contracts; all source proofs remain ordered dependencies. Ordinary context records retain their existing encoding. Fresh-store export is byte-identical and citation closure retains the introduction (`test:integration:decision-certified-citation-closure`), (`rule:cas:decision-certified-frame`).

**Rule (Certified membership in local selection)** · `rule:cas:decision-certified-selection`

In a certified frame, `Task::Select` consumes an explicit checked membership premise for that exact frame and its full admitted region. `CaseSelect` cites the original introduction for unique partition ownership and checks local definedness of the actual selected value, retaining the certified slot and source hypotheses (`rule:cas:decision-certified-frame`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-selection-needs-membership`). A value defined nowhere on that region refuses as `RefutedDomain`; a nonuniform countercell that source assumptions may exclude remains pending (`test:integration:decision-certified-selection-local-definedness`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-selection-conditional-countercell`). Unsupported refinement remains pending and this membership supplies no elimination cover (`rule:cas:decision-introduction-refusals`).

