Portable import reconstructs the original source proofs, partition, cut and enclosure checks in the receiving store before admitting the frame; a source-store citation alone cannot authorize a fresh receiver (`rule:cas:decision-introduction-wire`). This explains why fresh import costs more Work than introduction in each fixture. The new certificate family owns no cache; identical context interning shares its graph record but still pays validation and lookup. Citation closure costs 625 Work and 600 staged/output bytes for integer and sign, or 906 Work and 864 staged/output bytes for phase. Literal resource twins cover Work, staging, retained graph payload and returned output, including 37 prior Work and 257 retained caller bytes (`test:integration:decision-introduction-resources-integer`), (`test:integration:decision-introduction-resources-sign`), (`test:integration:decision-introduction-resources-phase`).

