Citing the retained partition reduces the integer-surrogate request to 383,318 generation and 1,353,635 checker Work, with a 3,186-byte witness; sign requires 124,250 and 594,593 Work with a 1,844-byte witness. The minimum successful generation allowances are 376,470 and 118,744 because optional response-envelope work can be omitted. Staged thresholds are 162,478 and 159,172 bytes; retained payload thresholds are 92,422 and 45,336 bytes. Phase selection remains `PendingPremise` at the exact-region boundary after 127,532 generation Work, requiring 90,427 staged and 87,846 retained bytes. Defaults and ordinary baseline pins are unchanged (`test:integration:decision-certified-selection-costs`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-selection-boundaries`), (`test:integration:decision-baseline-costs`).

**Theorem (Certified membership nonzero consequence)** · `thm:cas:decision-membership-nonzero`

Formal schema `decision.membership-nonzero`, version 1. Certified strict positive or negative membership makes the identical free coordinate defined and nonzero. Required premises: Exact certified membership slot and its checked local membership premise, strict selected guard and unchanged subject, retaining every source hypothesis. Standing: Lemma; instances are CAS-checked.

**Theorem (Original nonzero requirement discharge)** · `thm:cas:decision-nonzero-discharge`

Formal schema `decision.nonzero-discharge`, version 1. A checked certified sign consequence discharges one original nonzero requirement without changing the local equality or its retained requirements. Required premises: Original conditional defined-and-equal statement with exactly one pointwise nonzero residual and a checked decision.membership-nonzero fact on the identical context, region and predicate, retaining every source hypothesis. Standing: Lemma; instances are CAS-checked.

**Rule (Certified sign and original reciprocal)** · `rule:cas:decision-certified-sign`

`Certificate::DecisionNonZero(HypothesisRef)` under `RegionDecide` consumes one checked local membership premise from a certified ancestor slot zero and proves `NonZero` of the identical free Real coordinate under a strict positive or negative selected guard. `Certificate::DecisionDischarge` under `ContextClose` consumes the original conditional equality and this checked consequence, preserves its statement and requirements, clears exactly one matching pointwise residual and retains both the qualified membership and all source hypotheses (`thm:cas:decision-membership-nonzero`), (`thm:cas:decision-nonzero-discharge`). Certificate tags 15 and 16 carry semantic version 1 and are independently replayed. Zero, ordinary membership, sibling or escaped slots, widened regions and changed subjects refuse; altered original statements and unmatched guards cannot be discharged (`test:integration:decision-certified-sign-refusals`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-sign-zero-refusal`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-sign-ordinary-refusal`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-sign-discharge-refusals`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-sign-wire-versions`).

