**Rule (Declared native Integer results)** · `rule:cas:integer-case-results`

`CasesDraft::sort` declares the exact result sort before admission; every arm must match, including the first, and mixed Real/Integer arms refuse with `SymbolSortMismatch` atomically (`test:integration:integer-case-declared-results`). `AtomicSort::Integer` is an existing atomic value sort with exact integral rational literals, free declarations and explicit bound slots; it has no registered scalar ambient or placement edge (`test:integration:integer-case-literal-contract`), (`test:integration:integer-case-bound-result`). Scalar spaces remain Real and Complex as described in `docs/design/cas-symbol-sorts.md`. Finite integer cuts and partitions consume Integer options directly, and certified selection retains the exact Integer 3 for the 51/16 surrogate (`test:integration:decision-cut-integer-result`), (`test:integration:decision-certified-selection-costs`).

