`Cas::validate_lattice_basis` authenticates the local admission against its original matrix, offset and context handles. A unimodular shear or Integer lattice offset shift preserves the point set but refuses that identity check, as do foreign stores and changed contexts (`test:integration:lattice-basis-identities`). Ordinary witness export and expected-judgment replay reconstruct the determinant and both inverse identities in a fresh store; independently true identities for changed bases, offsets or contexts refuse reuse, and parameter replay retains its original hypothesis scope (`test:integration:lattice-basis-replay`), (`test:integration:lattice-basis-parameters`). These are basis witnesses under (`rule:cas:lattice-basis-admission`); range admission and its portable affine cover are specified by (`rule:cas:lattice-index-domains`), (`rule:cas:lattice-cover`); target attachment remains open.

